Noun vocabulary attribution
==========================

Source: National Institute of the Korean Language (formerly National Institute
of Korean Language Research), Korean Learners' Vocabulary List, May 2003.
Publication and reuse notice:
https://www.korean.go.kr/front_eng/down/down_02V.do?etc_seq=70&pageIndex=1

The publication states that this work may be used under Korea Open Government
License (KOGL), Type 1, with specific source attribution. Preserve this notice
when redistributing the selected vocabulary, derived tables or test data.
The source organization does not endorse this project or its stemming results.

Modifications: selected A-level noun entries with at least two Hangul syllables,
excluded cross-POS homographs found in that list and already supported bases,
separated historical homonym numbers, sorted and deduplicated spellings for
stemming, and generated subject/object-particle examples and negative tests.
The 379 source entries yield 377 additional spellings. Their 2002 frequency
ranks are historical; current dictionary standardness has not been verified.
Original file SHA-256 and retrieval details are recorded in source.json.

This data attribution is additional to the repository's software COPYING.
Do not replace it with an assertion that the selected data was hand-authored
or independently licensed solely under the Snowball software license.
